      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has many unused imports and lacks explanatory context. I'll improve understandability by trimming the dead imports and adding focused comments that explain the intent of each test.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed ~50 unused imports (leaving only the 8 actually needed), dropped the unused `MAX_LENGTH` constant, added a class-level Javadoc comment, and added a short inline comment to each test method explaining its intent — particularly splitting the serialization test body into two labeled sections (\"Serialize to bytes\" / \"Deserialize and confirm value equality\") to make the round-trip pattern immediately clear."
